    "title": "OHSAA girls basketball | Hall of Famer Paul Wackerly to become Green High School coach - NewsBreak",
    "text": "A Ohio high school basketball hall of fame coach will look to keep one of the area's top girls programs on top of its game. Longtime Stark County coach Paul Wackerly has been named the next girls basketball coach at Green High School. He replaces Alicia Manning, who resigned in June to return to her native Georgia . Wackerly won 526 games in 33 seasons as the head girls basketball coach at St. Thomas Aquinas, Hoover and GlenOak and as the head boys coach at Perry. He was inducted into the Ohio High School Basketball Coaches Association Hall of Fame in April. The association also honored him as a Century Award winner in recognition of achieving 500 career wins. Wackerly led Hoover to a Division I state championship in 2002 and GlenOak to back-to-back state berths in 2019 and 2020. His teams have won 10 district titles. Manning built Green into one of the area's most successful girls programs in her six seasons as head coach. The Bulldogs reached the Division II regional finals before losing to Olmsted Falls this past season. On X: @mpopovichREP | On Instagram: mike_popovich | On TikTok: mikepopovich This article originally appeared on The Repository: OHSAA girls basketball | Hall of Famer Paul Wackerly to become Green High School coach",
